housands second)=15 +1=16 \u21926, carryover1\n\nThen the final carryover 1. So the total is 1,611,745?\n\nWait, but when I add 791,763 + 819,982:\n\nLet me compute 791,763 + 800,000 = 1,591,763\n\nThen add 19,982: 1,591,763 +19,982 = 1,611,745. Yes, that matches. So the answer should be 1,611,745.\n\nWait, but let me check once more with another method. Let me write both numbers:\n\n791,763\n\n+819,982\n\nAdding each digit:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 3+2=5\n\nTens:6+8=14 \u2192 4, carryover 1\n\nHundreds:7+9=16 +1=17 \u21927, carryover1\n\nThousands:1+9=10 +1=11 \u21921, carryover1\n\nTen-thousands:9+1=10 +1=11 \u21921, carryover1\n\nHundred-thousands:7+8=15 +1=16 \u21926, carryover1\n\nMillions place: the carryover 1.\n\nSo the digits from right to left are 5,4,7,1,1,6,1. So the number is 1,611,745. Yes, that's correct.\n\nTherefore, the final answer is 1,611,745.\n</think>\n\n",
