g the thousands place, it's 1 (from first number) and 4 (from second number). So 1 + 4 = 5, plus the carried over 1 from the hundreds place (which was 11, so carried 1). Wait, the hundreds place was 8 + 2 + 1 (carry from tens?) Wait, let me redo the addition step by step carefully.\n\nStarting over:\n\nOnes place: 9 + 4 = 13. Write 3, carry 1.\n\nTens place: 6 + 9 = 15, plus 1 is 16. Write 6, carry 1.\n\nHundreds place: 8 + 2 = 10, plus 1 is 11. Write 1, carry 1.\n\nThousands place: 1 (from first number) + 4 (from second number) = 5, plus the carried 1 makes 6. So that's 6, no carry.\n\nTen thousands place: 7 + 7 = 14. Write 4, carry 1.\n\nHundred thousands place: 6 + 4 = 10, plus the carried 1 is 11. So 11.\n\nPutting all together: 1,1 (hundred thousands), 4 (ten thousands), 6 (thousands), 1 (hundreds), 6 (tens), 3 (ones). Wait, that would be 1,146,163. Hmm, but let me confirm with another method. Maybe adding the numbers in parts.\n\nAlternatively, 671,869 + 474,294.\n\nBreaking it down:\n\n600,000 + 400,000 = 1,000,000\n\n70,000 + 70,000 = 140,000 \u2192 total so far 1,140,000\n\n1,000 + 4,000 = 5,000 \u2192 1,145,000\n\n800 + 200 = 1,000 \u2192 1,146,000\n\n60 + 90 = 150 \u2192 1,146,150\n\n9 +4 =13 \u2192 total 1,146,163. Okay, that matches. So the answer should be 1,146,163. I think that's correct. Let me just do a quick check using another method, like estimating:\n\n671,869 is approximately 670,000 and 474,294 is approximately 470,000. Adding those gives 1,140,000. The actual sum is 1,146,163, which is 6,163 more, which makes sense because we rounded down both numbers. So that seems reasonable. Alright, I think that's the right answer.\n</think>\n\n",
