(ones). Wait, but let me structure that properly.\n\nWait, the places are:\n\nMillions: 1 (from the carryover)\n\nHundred thousands: 5 (since 15 in hundred thousands is 1 million and 5 hundred thousand)\n\nTen thousands: 3\n\nThousands:6\n\nHundreds:0\n\nTens:1\n\nOnes:0\n\nSo putting it all together: 1,536,010?\n\nWait, let me check with another method. Maybe adding the numbers in parts.\n\n670,659 + 865,351.\n\nLet me break them into 600,000 + 70,000 + 600 + 50 +9 and 800,000 +60,000 +5,000 +300 +50 +1.\n\nAdding each part:\n\n600,000 +800,000 =1,400,000\n\n70,000 +60,000 =130,000\n\n600 +5,000 =5,600\n\n300 +50 +50 =400? Wait, maybe this is getting confusing. Alternatively, maybe adding 670,659 + 800,000 =1,470,659, then add 65,351 (since 865,351 is 800k +65,351). Wait, perhaps that's better.\n\nWait, 670,659 + 865,351.\n\nLet me add 670,659 + 800,000 first: that's 1,470,659.\n\nThen add the remaining 65,351 to that.\n\n1,470,659 +65,351.\n\nAdding 1,470,659 +60,000 =1,530,659.\n\nThen add 5,351: 1,530,659 +5,000 =1,535,659, then +351 =1,536,010. \n\nOkay, so that matches the previous result. So the total is 1,536,010. \n\nTherefore, the answer should be 1,536,010. Let me confirm once more with straight addition:\n\n670,659\n\n+865,351\n\nAdding digit by digit:\n\nOnes:9+1=10 \u2192 0, carryover 1.\n\nTens:5+5=10 +1=11 \u21921, carryover1.\n\nHundreds:6+3=9 +1=10 \u21920, carryover1.\n\nThousands:0+5=5 +1=6 \u21926.\n\nTen thousands:7+6=13 \u21923, carryover1.\n\nHundred thousands:6+8=14 +1=15 \u21925, carryover1.\n\nMillions: the carryover 1.\n\nSo writing it out: 1 (million), 5 (hundred thousand), 3 (ten thousand), 6 (thousand), 0 (hundred), 1 (ten), 0 (one). So 1,536,010. Yep, that's correct. I think that's right. So the final answer is 1,536,010.\n</think>\n\n",
