1. Then the million's place is that 1. \n\nSo combining all digits: 1 (million), 0 (hundred thousand), 5 (ten thousand), 1 (thousand), 8 (hundred), 6 (ten), 8 (one). So 1,051,868. That seems right. \n\nAlternatively, maybe adding them another way to confirm. Let's see:\n\n470,434 + 581,434. Let's break it down:\n\n400,000 + 500,000 = 900,000\n\n70,000 + 80,000 = 150,000 \u2192 total so far 1,050,000\n\n400 + 400 = 800 \u2192 1,050,800\n\n30 + 30 = 60 \u2192 1,050,860\n\n4 +4 =8 \u2192 1,050,868. Wait, but that's different from the previous total. Wait, hold on, maybe I messed up the breakdown.\n\nWait, let me do it properly:\n\n470,434 is 400,000 + 70,000 + 400 + 30 +4\n\n581,434 is 500,000 + 80,000 + 1,000 + 400 + 30 +4\n\nAdding each part:\n\n400k +500k =900k\n\n70k +80k =150k \u2192 total 1,050k\n\n1,000 (from the second number) \u2192 1,051,000\n\n400 +400 =800 \u2192 1,051,800\n\n30+30=60 \u2192 1,051,860\n\n4+4=8 \u2192 1,051,868. Okay, so that matches the first method. So the answer is correct. \n\nI think I made a mistake in my first breakdown when I thought there was a discrepancy, but actually, when I broke it down again correctly, it's the same. So the final answer should be 1,051,868.\n</think>\n\n",
