ethod. Let's see, 107,840 + 286,204. If I round 107,840 to 108,000 and 286,204 to 286,200, then adding those gives 394,200. But since I rounded up by 160, I need to subtract that from the total. 394,200 - 160 = 394,040. Wait, that's close but not exactly the same. Hmm, maybe my rounding method is off. Alternatively, maybe I made a mistake here. Let me recalculate the rounded numbers.\n\nWait, 107,840 rounded to the nearest thousand is 108,000 (since 840 is more than 500). The second number, 286,204 rounded to the nearest thousand would be 286,000 (since 204 is less than 500). So adding 108,000 + 286,000 = 394,000. The actual numbers are 107,840 (which is 108,000 - 160) and 286,204 (which is 286,000 + 204). So total difference is -160 +204 = +44. Therefore, 394,000 +44 = 394,044. Okay, that matches my previous result. So that's a good check. \n\nTherefore, the answer should be 394,044.\n</think>\n\n",
