places. Let me write it out vertically:\n\n      531111\n    +818308\n    ---------\nStarting from the right:\nOnes: 1 + 8 = 9\nTens: 1 + 0 = 1\nHundreds: 1 + 3 = 4\nThousands: 1 + 8 = 9\nTen thousands: 3 + 1 = 4\nHundred thousands: 5 + 8 = 13. So write down 3 and carry over 1. Then the millions place is that 1. \n\nSo combining all digits: 1 (million), 3 (hundred thousand), 4 (ten thousand), 9 (thousand), 4 (hundred), 1 (ten), 9 (one). So 1,349,419. That seems right. \n\nAlternatively, maybe I should add them numerically without breaking it down:\n\n531,111 + 818,308. Let's see:\n\n531,111 + 800,000 is 1,331,111. Then add 18,308 more: 1,331,111 + 18,308 = 1,349,419. Yep, same result. Okay, that checks out. So the answer should be 1,349,419.\n</think>\n\n",
