ns digit is 1. So the total should be 1,438,936?\n\nWait, let me verify each step again to make sure I didn't make a mistake. Let me write it out vertically:\n\n      460552\n    +978384\n    ---------\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 2 + 4 = 6 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nTens: 5 + 8 = 13. Write 3, carry 1 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nHundreds: 5 + 3 = 8 + 1 (carry) = 9 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nThousands: 0 + 8 = 8 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nTen thousands: 6 + 7 = 13. Write 3, carry 1 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nHundred thousands: 4 + 9 = 13 + 1 (carry) = 14. So write 4 and carry 1. \n\nMillions place: The carryover 1. So total is 1,438,936. \n\nHmm, but let me add them another way to confirm. Maybe breaking them into parts.\n\n460,552 + 978,384. Let's split into 400,000 + 60,000 + 500 + 50 + 2 and 900,000 + 70,000 + 8,000 + 300 + 80 +4. Adding each part:\n\n400,000 + 900,000 = 1,300,000\n\n60,000 +70,000 = 130,000 \u2192 total so far 1,430,000\n\n500 + 8,000 = 8,500 \u2192 total 1,438,500\n\n50 + 300 = 350 \u2192 1,438,850\n\n2 +80 +4 = 86 \u2192 total 1,438,936. \n\nOkay, that matches. So the answer should be 1,438,936. I think that's correct. Let me check once more with another method. Maybe adding 460,552 + 978,384.\n\nAlternatively, 460,552 + 978,384. Let's add 460,552 + 900,000 first, which is 1,360,552. Then add 78,384 to that. 1,360,552 + 70,000 = 1,430,552. Then add 8,384: 1,430,552 + 8,000 = 1,438,552, then +384 gives 1,438,936. Yep, same result. So I think that's right.\n</think>\n\n",
