\n6 (ones)\n\n701,235:\n\n700,000 (hundred thousands)\n\n1,000 (thousands)\n\n200 (hundreds)\n\n30 (tens)\n\n5 (ones)\n\nSo adding each corresponding place:\n\nHundred thousands: 300k +700k =1,000,000\n\nTen thousands: 10k +0 (since second number has no ten thousands place) =10,000\n\nThousands:5k +1k =6,000\n\nHundreds:700 +200 =900\n\nTens:50 +30 =80\n\nOnes:6 +5 =11\n\nNow add all these together:\n\n1,000,000 +10,000 =1,010,000\n\n1,010,000 +6,000 =1,016,000\n\n1,016,000 +900 =1,016,900\n\n1,016,900 +80 =1,016,980\n\n1,016,980 +11 =1,016,991\n\nAh, there we go! I must have made an error in my previous expanded form breakdown. So that gives the same result as before, 1,016,991. Okay, so that confirms it again. So the correct answer is 1,016,991. I think my initial calculation was right, and the second method had a miscalculation which I corrected. So I'm confident now.\n</think>\n\n",
