      "text": " Okay, so I need to add 315,756 and 701,235. Let me start by writing them down one on top of the other, aligning the digits properly. \n\nFirst, I'll line up the numbers by their place values:\n\n```\n  315756\n+ 701235\n---------\n```\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit, which is the ones place. The ones digits are 6 and 5. Adding those gives 6 + 5 = 11. Hmm, that's more than 10, so I need to carry over. I'll write down 1 in the ones place and carry over 1 to the tens column.\n\nNext, the tens place. The digits here are 5 and 3, plus the carried-over 1. So 5 + 3 = 8, plus 1 makes 9. No carry-over here. So the tens place is 9.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place. The digits are 7 and 2. 7 + 2 = 9. So that's straightforward, 9 in the hundreds place.\n\nNow the thousands place. The digits here are 5 and 1. 5 + 1 = 6. So that's 6 in the thousands place.\n\nNext up is the ten thousands place. The digits are 1 and 0. 1 + 0 = 1. So that's 1 in the ten thousands place.\n\nFinally, the hundred thousands place. The digits are 3 and 7. 3 + 7 = 10. Wait, that's 10? So that would be 0 in the hundred thousands place and carry over 1 to the millions place. But since there are no more digits, that carried-over 1 becomes a 1 in the millions place.\n\nPutting it all together, starting from the right: ones is 1, tens 9, hundreds 9, thousands 6, ten thousands 1, hundred thousands 0, and then the 1 in the millions. So the total should be 1,016,991.\n\nWait, let me check again to make sure I didn't make a mistake. Let me add them another way. Maybe breaking them into parts. \n\n315,756 + 700,000 is 1,015,756. Then add the remaining 1,235. 1,015,756 + 1,235. Let's see: 1,015,756 + 1,000 is 1,016,756. Then add 235: 1,016,756 + 235 = 1,016,991. Okay, that matches. So the answer should be correct.\n\nAlternatively, adding digit by digit again step by step:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 6 +5 =11. Write 1, carryover 1.\n\nTens:5+3=8 +1=9. No carryover.\n\nHundreds:7+2=9.\n\nThousands:5+1=6.\n\nTen thousands:1+0=1.\n\nHundred thousands:3+7=10. So write 0 and carryover 1. Since there are no more digits, add the 1 in the millions place. So yes, 1,016,991. \n\nI think that's right. Let me confirm once more with another method. Maybe using expanded form.\n\n315,756 = 300,000 + 10,000 + 5,000 + 700 + 50 +6\n\n701,235 = 700,000 + 1,000 + 200 + 30 +5\n\nAdding each part:\n\n300,000 +700,000 = 1,000,000\n\n10,000 +1,000 =11,000\n\n5,000 +200 =5,200\n\n700 +30 =730\n\n50 +5 =55\n\n6 +0=6 (since the second number has no more digits there)\n\nNow add all those together:\n\n1,000,000 +11,000 =1,011,000\n\n1,011,000 +5,200 =1,016,200\n\n1,016,200 +730 =1,016,930\n\n1,016,930 +55 =1,016,985\n\nWait, hold on, that's different. Wait, 1,016,930 +55 is 1,016,985? But that contradicts the previous result. Hmm, where did I go wrong here?\n\nWait, let me check the expanded form again. Maybe I made a mistake in breaking it down.\n\nOriginal numbers:\n\n315,756:\n\n300,000 (hundred thousands)\n\n10,000 (ten thousands)\n\n5,000 (thousands)\n\n700 (hundreds)\n\n50 (tens)\n\n6 (ones)\n\n701,235:\n\n700,000 (hundred thousands)\n\n1,000 (thousands)\n\n200 (hundreds)\n\n30 (tens)\n\n5 (ones)\n\nWait, so when adding the thousands place in the second number: 701,235 has 1 thousand, so 1,000. But in the first number, 315,756 has 5 thousands (since 315,756 is 300k +10k +5k +...). So 5,000 +1,000 =6,000. Wait, but in the expanded form breakdown above, when adding the thousands parts, I had 5,000 +200? Wait no, that's a mistake. Wait, the thousands place in the second number is 1,000, so the thousands parts should be 5,000 +1,000 =6,000. But in my previous breakdown, I wrote 5,000 +200 =5,200. That's incorrect. The 200 is the hundreds place of the second number. So I messed up the breakdown.\n\nLet me redo the expanded form correctly:\n\n315,756:\n\n300,000 (hundred thousands)\n\n10,000 (ten thousands)\n\n5,000 (thousands)\n\n700 (hundreds)\n\n50 (tens)\n\n6 (ones)\n\n701,235:\n\n700,000 (hundred thousands)\n\n1,000 (thousands)\n\n200 (hundreds)\n\n30 (tens)\n\n5 (ones)\n\nNow adding each corresponding place:\n\nHundred thousands: 300k +700k =1,000,000\n\nTen thousands: 10k +0 (since second number has 0 in ten thousands place?) Wait, 701,235 is 700,000 +1,000 +200 +30 +5. So the ten thousands place in the second number is 0. So 10k +0 =10,000.\n\nThousands place: 5,000 +1,000 =6,000\n\nHundreds place:700 +200 =900\n\nTens place:50 +30 =80\n\nOnes place:6 +5 =11\n\nNow adding all these together:\n\n1,000,000 +10,000 =1,010,000\n\n1,010,000 +6,000 =1,016,000\n\n1,016,000 +900 =1,016,900\n\n1,016,900 +80 =1,016,980\n\n1,016,980 +11 =1,016,991\n\nAh, there we go. So that matches the previous result. I must have misassigned the thousands place in my first expanded form breakdown. So the correct total is indeed 1,016,991. Okay, so that confirms it again. I think that's solid now. So the answer is correct.\n\nAnother way: using calculator-like addition step by step:\n\n315756\n\n+701235\n\nStart from the right:\n\nOnes:6+5=11. Write down 1, carryover 1.\n\nTens:5+3=8 +1=9. Write 9, no carryover.\n\nHundreds:7+2=9. Write 9.\n\nThousands:5 (from first number) +1 (from second) =6. Write 6.\n\nTen thousands:1 (from first number's ten thousands place) +0 (since second number has 0 there) =1. Write 1.\n\nHundred thousands:3 +7=10. Write 0, carryover 1.\n\nMillions place: the carried over 1. So total is 1,016,991.\n\nYes, that's consistent. I think I've verified it multiple ways. So the final answer is correct.\n</think>\n\n",
