\n= ?\n\nLet me break it down:\n\nFirst, add the thousands: 800,000 + 100,000 = 900,000.\n\nThen the hundreds: 64,000 + 5,000 = 69,000.\n\nNext, the tens: 831 + 986. Wait, 831 + 986. Let's compute that separately. 800 + 900 = 1,700. 31 +86 = 117. So total is 1,700 + 117 = 1,817. \n\nAdding all parts together: 900,000 + 69,000 = 969,000. Then 969,000 + 1,817 = 970,817. Okay, that matches. So the answer should be 970,817. Let me check once more with column addition:\n\n  864831\n+105986\n--------\nStarting from the right:\n1+6=7\n3+8=11 (write 1, carry 1)\n8+9+1=18 (write 8, carry 1)\n4+5+1=10 (write 0, carry 1)\n6+0+1=7\n8+1=9\nSo yes, 970817. Looks correct.\n</think>\n\n",
