ands: 50k + 20k = 70k\nThousands: 5k + 1k = 6k\nHundreds: 600 + 200 = 800\nTens: 0 + 90 = 90\n\nAdding all those together: 800,000 + 70,000 = 870,000; plus 6,000 is 876,000; plus 800 is 876,800; plus 90 is 876,890. Yep, that matches. So the answer should be 876,890. I think that's correct. Let me just do a quick check using another way, maybe rounding:\n\n355,600 is approximately 355,600, and 521,290 is about 521,300. Adding those approximations gives 355,600 + 521,300 = 876,900. But since I rounded 521,290 up by 10, the actual sum should be 10 less, which is 876,890. That checks out. Okay, so I'm confident the answer is 876,890.\n</think>\n\n",
