es: 2 + 8 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\nTens: 5 + 5 = 10 + 1 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\nHundreds: 5 +5 =10 +1 =11 \u21921, carry1\n\nThousands:4 +4 =8 +1=9 \u21929, no carry\n\nTen thousands:5 +9=14 \u21924, carry1\n\nHundred thousands:8 +8=16 +1=17 \u21927, carry1\n\nMillions: the carryover 1.\n\nSo combining all digits: 1 (million), 7 (hundred thousand), 4 (ten thousand), 9 (thousand), 1 (hundred), 1 (ten), 0 (one). So that's 1,749,110. \n\nWait, but let me confirm with another method. Maybe adding the numbers in parts. \n\n854,552 + 894,558. Let's break them into 800,000 + 54,552 and 800,000 + 94,558. \n\nAdding the 800k +800k = 1,600,000. Then 54,552 +94,558. \n\n54,552 +94,558: \n\n54,552 +90,000 =144,552\n\nThen add 4,558: 144,552 +4,558 = 149,110. \n\nSo total is 1,600,000 +149,110 =1,749,110. \n\nSame result. Okay, that seems right. So the answer should be 1,749,110.\n</think>\n\n",
