e each digit:\n\nFirst number: 7 (hundred thousands), 4 (ten thousands), 7 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 7 (ones).\n\nSecond number:9 (hundred thousands),1 (ten thousands),5 (thousands),7 (hundreds),0 (tens),7 (ones).\n\nAdding each column from right to left:\n\nOnes: 7 +7 =14. Write down 4, carryover 1.\n\nTens:1 +0 =1 +1 (carryover) =2. Write 2, no carryover.\n\nHundreds:8 +7=15. Write 5, carryover 1.\n\nThousands:7 +5=12 +1=13. Write 3, carryover 1.\n\nTen thousands:4 +1=5 +1=6. Write 6, no carryover.\n\nHundred thousands:7 +9=16. Write 6, carryover 1.\n\nMillions: 0 +0 +1=1. Write 1.\n\nSo putting all together: 1,663,524.\n\nWait, but when I first thought I had 1,763,524? Hmm, no, let me check again:\n\nWait, the thousands place: first number's thousands digit is 7, second is 5. 7+5=12, plus the carryover 1 from the hundreds place (which was 15, so carryover 1). So 12+1=13. So thousands digit is 3, carryover 1 to the next (ten thousands place).\n\nTen thousands place: first number's ten thousands is 4, second is 1. 4+1=5, plus the carryover 1 makes 6. So ten thousands is 6, no carryover.\n\nHundred thousands place: 7 +9 =16. So 6 with carryover 1. So hundred thousands is 6, carryover 1 to millions.\n\nMillions place: 1. So total is 1,663,524. \n\nWait, but let me add them numerically to confirm:\n\n747,817 + 915,707.\n\nLet me compute 747,817 + 900,000 = 1,647,817. Then add 15,707 more: 1,647,817 +15,707 = 1,663,524. Yes, that matches. So the correct answer is 1,663,524.\n\nI think my initial mistake was in the first calculation where I misaligned the digits, but upon redoing it step by step, it's clear. So the answer should be 1,663,524.\n</think>\n\n",
