 from the right:\n\nOnes: 7 + 7 = 14? Wait, no, the second number's ones digit is 0. Wait, original numbers: 747,817 and 915,707. Let me confirm:\n\nFirst number: 747,817. Breaking down:\n\n- Millions: 0 (since it's a 6-digit number)\n- Hundred thousands: 7\n- Ten thousands: 4\n- Thousands: 7\n- Hundreds: 8\n- Tens: 1\n- Ones: 7\n\nSecond number: 915,707:\n\n- Hundred thousands: 9\n- Ten thousands: 1\n- Thousands: 5\n- Hundreds: 7\n- Tens: 0\n- Ones: 7\n\nWait, actually, let me write them properly aligned:\n\n      747817\n    +915707\n    ---------\n    \nLet me align each digit:\n\nMillions place: 0 (from first) and 0 (since second is 6 digits). Wait, actually, the second number is 915,707 which is 6 digits, so:\n\nWait, 747,817 is 7 (hundred thousand), 4 (ten thousand), 7 (thousand), 8 (hundred), 1 (ten), 7 (one).\n\n915,707 is 9 (hundred thousand), 1 (ten thousand), 5 (thousand), 7 (hundred), 0 (ten), 7 (one).\n\nSo when adding:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes place: 7 + 7 = 14. Wait, hold on! The first number's ones digit is 7, the second's is 7? Wait, original problem says 747817 and 915707. Let me check again:\n\nWait, 747,817: the digits are 7 (hundred thousands), 4 (ten thousands), 7 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 7 (ones).\n\n915,707: 9 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 5 (thousands), 7 (hundreds), 0 (tens), 7 (ones). \n\nAh! So the ones digits are both 7. So 7 +7 =14. So that's 4 in ones, carryover 1.\n\nThen tens place: first number has 1, second has 0. 1+0=1, plus the carryover 1 makes 2. So tens digit is 2, no carryover.\n\nHundreds place: 8 +7 =15. So 5 in hundreds, carryover 1.\n\nThousands place: 7 +5 =12, plus 1 is 13. So 3 in thousands, carryover 1.\n\nTen thousands place: 4 +1 =5, plus 1 is 6. So 6 in ten thousands, no carryover.\n\nHundred thousands place:7 +9 =16. So 6 in hundred thousands, carryover 1.\n\nMillions place: the carryover 1. So total is 1,663,524?\n\nWait, let me do this step by step again carefully:\n\nLet me write each digit:\n\nFirst number: 7 (hundred thousands), 4 (ten thousands), 7 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 7 (ones).\n\nSecond number:9 (hundred thousands),1 (ten thousands),5 (thousands),7 (hundreds),0 (tens),7 (ones).\n\nAdding each column from right to left:\n\nOnes: 7 +7 =14. Write down 4, carryover 1.\n\nTens:1 +0 =1 +1 (carryover) =2. Write 2, no carryover.\n\nHundreds:8 +7=15. Write 5, carryover 1.\n\nThousands:7 +5=12 +1=13. Write 3, carryover 1.\n\nTen thousands:4 +1=5 +1=6. Write 6, no carryover.\n\nHundred thousands:7 +9=16. Write 6, carryover 1.\n\nMillions: 0 +0 +1=1. Write 1.\n\nSo putting all together: 1,663,524.\n\nWait, but when I first thought I had 1,763,524? Hmm, no, let me check again:\n\nWait, the thousands place: first number's thousands digit is 7, second is 5. 7+5=12, plus the carryover 1 from the hundreds place (which was 15, so carryover 1). So 12+1=13. So thousands digit is 3, carryover 1 to the next (ten thousands place).\n\nTen thousands place: first number's ten thousands is 4, second is 1. 4+1=5, plus the carryover 1 makes 6. So ten thousands is 6, no carryover.\n\nHundred thousands place: 7 +9 =16. So 6 with carryover 1. So hundred thousands is 6, carryover 1 to millions.\n\nMillions place: 1. So total is 1,663,524. \n\nWait, but let me add them numerically to confirm:\n\n747,817 + 915,707.\n\nLet me compute 747,817 + 900,000 = 1,647,817. Then add 15,707 more: 1,647,817 +15,707 = 1,663,524. Yes, that matches. So the correct answer is 1,663,524.\n\nI think my initial mistake was in the first calculation where I misaligned the digits, but upon redoing it step by step, it's clear. So the answer should be 1,663,524.\n</think>\n\n",
