kes 12. So the digits are 12 followed by 0, 0, 1, 3, 2. Wait, maybe I need to write it out again:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 2, carryover 1\nTens: 3, carryover 1\nHundreds: 1, carryover 1\nThousands: 0, carryover 1\nTen thousands: 0, carryover 1\nHundred thousands: 12. \n\nSo putting all together, the digits from right to left are 2 (ones), 3 (tens), 1 (hundreds), 0 (thousands), 0 (ten thousands), and then 12 in the hundred thousands. But since 12 is two digits, the 1 would be in the millions place. So actually, the total should be 1,200,132. Let me confirm with another method. Maybe adding the numbers in parts.\n\n698,259 + 500,000 is 1,198,259. Then add 1,873: 1,198,259 + 1,873 = 1,200,132. Yep, that matches. Okay, so the answer is correct.\n</think>\n\n",
