nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes place: 1 + 9 = 10. Write 0, carryover 1. Correct.\n\nTens place: 7 + 0 =7 +1 (carryover) =8. Correct.\n\nHundreds place: 7 + 2 =9. Correct.\n\nThousands place: 6 + 2 =8. Correct.\n\nTen thousands place: 1 (from 216,771) + 6 (from 362,209) =7. Correct.\n\nHundred thousands place: 2 +3 =5. So combining all digits: 5 7 8 9 8 0. That's 578,980. Wait, so why did I think it was 579,880 before? Oh, I must have miswritten the digits. So the correct sum is 578,980. \n\nWait, but when I broke it down into parts, I also got 578,980. So my first calculation was correct, but when I first thought I had 579,880, that was a mistake in writing the digits. So the correct answer is 578,980. Let me confirm once more with another method.\n\nAlternatively, adding 216,771 + 362,209:\n\n216,771 + 362,209. Let's add 216,771 + 300,000 = 516,771. Then add 62,209. 516,771 + 60,000 = 576,771. Then +2,209: 576,771 + 2,209 = 578,980. Yes, that matches. So the correct answer is 578,980. I must have made a typo in my first conclusion. So the step-by-step addition was correct, but when I wrote the final digits, I might have mixed up the places. Let me check the digit positions again:\n\nAfter adding each place:\n\nHundred thousands: 5\n\nTen thousands:7\n\nThousands:8\n\nHundreds:9\n\nTens:8\n\nOnes:0\n\nSo that's 5 (hundred thousands), 7 (ten thousands), 8 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 8 (tens), 0 (ones). So 578,980. Correct. So the initial mistake was a miscalculation when I thought I had 579,880. So the correct answer is 578,980.\n</think>\n\n",
