\nSo the number is 1,232,799. Wait, but when I first thought I had 1,232,800. So where did I go wrong?\n\nWait, maybe I miscalculated the thousands place. Let me check the thousands digit again. The first number is 767,914. Breaking down:\n\n7 (hundred thousands), 6 (ten thousands), 7 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 4 (ones).\n\nSecond number:464,885 is 4 (hundred thousands), 6 (ten thousands),4 (thousands),8 (hundreds),8 (tens),5 (ones).\n\nSo thousands place digits are 7 and 4. 7+4=11, plus the carryover 1 from hundreds place (which was 17, so carryover 1). So 11+1=12. So thousands digit is 2, carryover 1. Correct.\n\nTen thousands place: 6 +6 =12 +1=13. So 3, carryover 1. Correct.\n\nHundred thousands:7+4=11 +1=12. So 2, carryover 1. Correct.\n\nSo the total is 1,232,799. Wait, but when I first added them in my head, I thought maybe 1,232,800. Hmm. Let me do the addition another way to verify.\n\nAlternatively, adding 767,914 + 464,885:\n\nLet me add 767,914 + 400,000 = 1,167,914\n\nThen add 64,885: 1,167,914 + 60,000 = 1,227,914\n\nThen +4,885: 1,227,914 +4,000 =1,231,914\n\nThen +885: 1,231,914 +885 =1,232,799. \n\nYes, so that's correct. So the correct answer is 1,232,799. Wait, but in my first calculation I thought 1,232,800. So I must have made a mistake in my initial thought. Therefore, the correct sum is 1,232,799. \n\nWait, but let me check with another method. Let's add the numbers digit by digit again:\n\n767,914\n\n+464,885\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes:4+5=9\n\nTens:1+8=9\n\nHundreds:9+8=17 (write 7, carryover 1)\n\nThousands:7+4=11 +1=12 (write 2, carryover1)\n\nTen thousands:6+6=12 +1=13 (write3, carryover1)\n\nHundred thousands:7+4=11 +1=12 (write2, carryover1)\n\nMillions:1\n\nSo the number is 1,232,799. So that's correct. Therefore, the answer should be 1,232,799. \n\nWait, but maybe I miscounted the places. Let me write the numbers with commas to check:\n\n767,914 is seven hundred sixty-seven thousand, nine hundred fourteen.\n\n464,885 is four hundred sixty-four thousand, eight hundred eighty-five.\n\nAdding them:\n\n700,000 + 400,000 = 1,100,000\n\n60,000 + 60,000 = 120,000 \u2192 total so far 1,220,000\n\n7,000 +4,000 =11,000 \u2192 total 1,231,000\n\n900 +800 =1,700 \u2192 total 1,232,700\n\n10 +80 =90 \u2192 total 1,232,790\n\n4 +5=9 \u2192 total 1,232,799. \n\nYes, that matches. So the correct answer is 1,232,799. I must have miscalculated earlier when I thought 800. So the final answer is 1,232,799. \n\nWait, but let me check with another approach. Let me use another method, like adding the numbers in parts:\n\n767,914 + 464,885\n\nBreak into 700,000 + 60,000 +7,000 +900 +10 +4\n\nand 400,000 +60,000 +4,000 +800 +80 +5\n\nAdding each part:\n\nMillions: 0 +0 =0 (but there will be a carryover)\n\nHundred thousands:700k +400k =1,100,000\n\nTen thousands:60k +60k =120k \u2192 total so far 1,220k\n\nThousands:7k +4k =11k \u2192 total 1,231k\n\nHundreds:900 +800 =1,700 \u2192 1,232,700\n\nTens:10 +80 =90 \u2192 1,232,790\n\nOnes:4+5=9 \u2192 total 1,232,799. \n\nYes, same result. So I think the correct answer is 1,232,799. Therefore, the initial mistake was probably a miscalculation when I first thought of 800 in the tens place, but actually the tens place was 9, so the final digits are correct. \n\nTherefore, the sum of 767,914 and 464,885 is 1,232,799.\n</think>\n\n",
