n that place, carryover 1. Correct.\n\nHundred-thousands place: 7 + 4 = 11, plus the carried-over 1 makes 12. So yes, 12 in the hundred-thousands place. So combining all digits: 1,2 (hundred-thousands), 8 (ten-thousands), 1 (thousands), 2 (hundreds), 9 (tens), 9 (ones). So 1,281,299.\n\nWait, but let me verify with another method. Maybe adding the numbers in parts. Let's break them down:\n\n783,244 can be 700,000 + 80,000 + 3,000 + 200 + 40 +4\n\n498,055 is 400,000 + 90,000 + 8,000 + 0 + 50 +5\n\nAdding each part:\n\n700,000 + 400,000 = 1,100,000\n\n80,000 + 90,000 = 170,000\n\n3,000 +8,000 = 11,000\n\n200 +0 = 200\n\n40 +50 =90\n\n4 +5 =9\n\nNow add all those together:\n\n1,100,000 + 170,000 = 1,270,000\n\n1,270,000 +11,000 = 1,281,000\n\n1,281,000 +200 = 1,281,200\n\n1,281,200 +90 = 1,281,290\n\n1,281,290 +9 =1,281,299\n\nOkay, that matches the previous result. So the sum is indeed 1,281,299. I think that's correct. Let me try another way, using column addition again to confirm.\n\nWriting it out vertically again:\n\n\u202f783244\n\n+498055\n\n----------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 4+5=9\n\nTens:4+5=9\n\nHundreds:2+0=2\n\nThousands:3+8=11 (write 1, carryover 1)\n\nTen-thousands:8+9+1=18 (write 8, carryover 1)\n\nHundred-thousands:7+4+1=12 (write 12)\n\nSo the total is 1,281,299. Yep, same as before. I think that's right. Maybe I can use a calculator to check, but since I can't, the two methods agree, so I'm confident.\n</think>\n\n",
