ce it's the hundred-thousands place, adding 9 and 9 gives 18. So we write 8 in the hundred-thousands place and carryover 1 to the millions place. Since there's no millions place in the original numbers, the carryover becomes a 1 in the millions place. So the total is 1 (million) 8 (hundred thousand) 6 (ten thousand) 8 (thousand) 7 (hundred) 0 (ten) 7 (one). So that's 1,868,707.\n\nWait, but when I broke it down earlier, I thought the ten thousands place was 5 +1 +1 (carryover) which would be 7, but in the breakdown, the ten thousands place is 5 (from first number) and 1 (from second number). So 5+1=6, plus no carryover from the thousands place (since thousands place had 4+3+carryover 1=8, so no carryover). So that's correct. So the ten thousands digit is 6. \n\nSo putting it all together, the sum is 1,868,707. Let me check with another method. Let's add 954,931 + 913,776.\n\nAlternatively, 954,931 + 900,000 = 1,854,931. Then subtract the difference: 913,776 is 900,000 +13,776. Wait, maybe that complicates. Alternatively, 954,931 + 913,776 = (900,000 + 54,931) + (900,000 +13,776) = 1,800,000 + (54,931 +13,776). Let's compute 54,931 +13,776:\n\n54,931 +10,000 =64,931; plus 3,776 = 68,707. So total is 1,800,000 +68,707 =1,868,707. Okay, that matches. So the answer should be 1,868,707. \n\nWait, but in my first calculation when I thought of the hundred-thousands place adding to 18, I thought maybe I made a mistake, but the cross-verification shows it's correct. So the final answer is 1,868,707. Let me just confirm once more with direct addition:\n\n954,931\n\n+913,776\n\nAdding digit by digit:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes:1+6=7\n\nTens:3+7=10 (0, carry 1)\n\nHundreds:9+7=16 +1=17 (7, carry1)\n\nThousands:4+3=7 +1=8 (8, no carry)\n\nTen-thousands:5+1=6\n\nHundred-thousands:9+9=18 (8, carry1)\n\nThen the carryover 1 becomes the millions place. So the number is 1,868,707. Yes, that's correct. So the answer is 1,868,707.\n</think>\n\n",
