ce):\n\n3 + 4 = 7. Write down 7.\n\nTens place: 2 + 7 = 9. Write down 9.\n\nHundreds place: 1 + 1 = 2. Write down 2.\n\nThousands place: 3 + 3 = 6. Write down 6.\n\nTen-thousands place: 3 (from first number) + 1 (from second number) = 4. Write down 4.\n\nHundred-thousands place: 6 + 2 = 8. Write down 8.\n\nWait, so putting it all together, the sum would be 846,297?\n\nWait, let me check again step by step to make sure I didn't make a mistake.\n\nStarting over:\n\nFirst number: 633,123\n\nSecond number: 213,174\n\nAdding digit by digit:\n\nOnes: 3 + 4 = 7\n\nTens: 2 + 7 = 9\n\nHundreds: 1 + 1 = 2\n\nThousands: 3 (from first number's thousands place) + 3 (second number's thousands place) = 6\n\nTen-thousands: 3 (from first number's ten-thousands) + 1 (second number's ten-thousands) = 4\n\nHundred-thousands: 6 + 2 = 8\n\nSo combining all digits: 8 (hundred thousands), 4 (ten thousands), 6 (thousands), 2 (hundreds), 9 (tens), 7 (ones). So 846,297.\n\nHmm, but let me verify with another method to be sure. Maybe adding the numbers in parts.\n\nBreaking down 633,123 + 213,174:\n\nFirst, add the hundred thousands: 600,000 + 200,000 = 800,000.\n\nThen the ten thousands: 30,000 + 10,000 = 40,000. Total so far: 840,000.\n\nThousands: 3,000 + 3,000 = 6,000. Total now 846,000.\n\nHundreds: 100 + 100 = 200. Total 846,200.\n\nTens: 20 + 70 = 90. Total 846,290.\n\nOnes: 3 +4 =7. Total 846,297. Okay, that matches.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using another approach: 633,123 + 200,000 = 833,123. Then add 13,174.\n\n833,123 +10,000 = 843,123. Then +3,000 = 846,123. Then +174: 846,123 +174 = 846,297. Yep, same result.\n\nSo the answer should be 846,297. Let me check once more with column addition:\n\n      633123\n    +213174\n    ---------\nStarting from the right:\n\n3+4=7\n\n2+7=9\n\n1+1=2\n\n3+3=6\n\n3+1=4\n\n6+2=8\n\nSo writing the digits: 8 4 6 2 9 7 \u2192 846,297. Correct.\n\nI think that's solid. No carrying over needed in any place since all the sums are under 10. So the final answer is 846,297.\n</think>\n\n",
