nds place: first number has 2 (thousands place), second has 2 (thousands place). Wait, no, hold on. Wait, the thousands place in the first number is the third digit from the right? Let me clarify:\n\nWait, maybe I messed up the place values. Let me write both numbers digit by digit:\n\n432,849:\nDigits from right (ones to hundred thousands):\nOnes: 9\nTens:4\nHundreds:8\nThousands:2\nTen thousands:3\nHundred thousands:4\n\n132,075:\nOnes:5\nTens:7\nHundreds:0\nThousands:2\nTen thousands:3\nHundred thousands:1\n\nSo when adding the thousands place: first number's thousands digit is 2, second's is 2. So 2 +2 =4. Wait, but earlier I thought the thousands place was 2 +7? Wait, no, that was a mistake. Wait, the thousands place is the fourth digit from the right. Let me re-express both numbers:\n\n432849:\nPositions (from right):\n1:9 (ones)\n2:4 (tens)\n3:8 (hundreds)\n4:2 (thousands)\n5:3 (ten thousands)\n6:4 (hundred thousands)\n\n132075:\n1:5 (ones)\n2:7 (tens)\n3:0 (hundreds)\n4:2 (thousands)\n5:3 (ten thousands)\n6:1 (hundred thousands)\n\nSo adding thousands place (position 4): 2 +2 =4. So that's correct. Then ten thousands place (position5): 3 +3=6. Hundred thousands:4+1=5. \n\nWait, so in my initial calculation, when I thought the thousands place was 2 +7, that was wrong. I must have confused the tens and thousands. Let me redo the addition step by step properly.\n\nStarting over:\n\nOnes place: 9 +5 =14. Write 4, carryover 1.\n\nTens place:4 +7 =11, plus 1 is 12. Write 2, carryover1.\n\nHundreds place:8 +0 +1=9. Write 9, no carryover.\n\nThousands place:2 +2 =4. Write 4.\n\nTen thousands place:3 +3=6. Write 6.\n\nHundred thousands place:4 +1=5. Write 5.\n\nSo putting all together: 5 (hundred thousands), 6 (ten thousands), 4 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 2 (tens), 4 (ones). So 564,924. Wait, but let me check with another method to confirm.\n\nAlternatively, adding 432,849 +132,075:\n\nLet me add 432,849 + 100,000 =532,849. Then add 32,075 more. 532,849 +30,000 =562,849. Then +2,075: 562,849 +2,000=564,849, then +75=564,924. Yes, same result. So the answer is 564,924. I think my initial mistake was when I first thought the thousands place had a 7, but that was the tens place. So the correct sum is 564,924.\n</think>\n\n",
