eds place was 1 +1, plus the carryover from the tens place which was already handled. Wait, let me go through each step again step by step to be sure.\n\nStarting over:\n\nOnes place: 2 +9 =11. Write 1, carryover 1.\n\nTens: 6 +5 =11 +1=12. Write 2, carryover 1.\n\nHundreds: 1 +1 =2 +1=3. Write 3, no carryover.\n\nThousands: 4 +0 =4. Write 4.\n\nTen thousands:7 +8=15. Write 5, carryover 1.\n\nHundred thousands:1 +1=2 +1=3. Write 3.\n\nSo combining all digits: 3 (hundred thousands), 5 (ten thousands), 4 (thousands), 3 (hundreds), 2 (tens), 1 (ones). So 354,321. Hmm, that seems correct. Let me add them using another method to confirm. \n\nAlternatively, adding 174,162 + 180,159. Let's break it down:\n\n174,162 + 180,159 = (174,000 + 162) + (180,000 + 159) \n\n= (174,000 + 180,000) + (162 + 159)\n\n= 354,000 + 321 \n\n= 354,321. \n\nYes, that matches. So the answer is correct.\n</think>\n\n",
