3,000.\n\nHundreds: 700 +900=1,600. Adding to 633,000 gives 634,600.\n\nTens: 30 +90=120. Adding gives 634,720.\n\nOnes:4 +3=7. Total 634,727. Okay, that matches. So the answer should be correct. \n\nI think that's right. Maybe I can also use another way, like rounding. Let's see:\n\n429,734 is close to 430,000. 204,993 is close to 205,000. Adding those gives 635,000. But since I rounded up by 266 and 267 respectively, total overestimation is 266 +267=533. So subtract that from 635,000: 635,000 -533=634,467. Wait, that's not matching. Hmm, maybe my rounding method is off here. Wait, perhaps I miscalculated the rounding.\n\nWait, 429,734 to 430,000 is an increase of 266 (since 430,000 -429,734=266). \n\n204,993 to 205,000 is an increase of 67 (205,000 -204,993=67). \n\nSo total overestimation is 266 +67=333. \n\nSo 635,000 -333=634,667. Hmm, that's different from the previous result. Wait, so now I'm confused. Did I make a mistake here?\n\nWait, maybe my rounding approach is not the best here. Let me check again. \n\nAlternatively, perhaps I made an arithmetic error in the rounding method. Let me recalculate:\n\n429,734 + 204,993 = ?\n\nIf I add 429,734 + 200,000 = 629,734. Then add the remaining 4,993: 629,734 +4,993. \n\n629,734 +4,000 =633,734. Then +993: 633,734 +993 = 634,727. Okay, that matches the first result. So the rounding method must have had an error. Probably messed up the overestimation numbers. \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 634,727. I think that's solid now. \n\nAnother way: Let's use column addition with the numbers written out:\n\n\u202f\u00a0429734\n\n+204993\n\n----------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 4+3=7\n\nTens:3+9=12, write 2, carryover 1\n\nHundreds:7+9=16 +1=17, write 7, carryover1\n\nThousands:9+4=13 +1=14, write4, carryover1\n\nTen thousands:2+0=2 +1=3\n\nHundred thousands:4+2=6\n\nSo the result is 634727. Yep, that's consistent. \n\nI think I've verified it multiple ways. The answer should be 634,727.\n</think>\n\n",
