be breaking the numbers into parts:\n\n724,912 + 196,515.\n\nLet's split into 700,000 + 24,912 and 100,000 + 96,515.\n\nWait, maybe adding 724,912 + 200,000 would be 924,912, but since it's 196,515, that's 200,000 minus 3,485. So 924,912 - 3,485 = ?\n\nWait, maybe that's more complicated. Alternatively, adding digit by digit again:\n\nLet me write it out vertically again:\n\n  724912\n+ 196515\n----------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 2 +5 =7\n\nTens:1+1=2\n\nHundreds:9+5=14 (write 4, carry 1)\n\nThousands:4 +6 =10, plus 1 is 11 (write 1, carry 1)\n\nTen-thousands:2 +9=11, plus 1 is 12 (write 2, carry 1)\n\nHundred-thousands:7 +1=8, plus 1 is 9.\n\nSo yes, that gives 921,427. Wait, but when I first thought of the answer, I thought maybe 921,427. Let me check with another method.\n\nAlternatively, adding 724,912 + 196,515:\n\n724,912 + 196,515.\n\nLet me add 724,912 + 200,000 first, which is 924,912. Then subtract the extra 3,485 (since 200,000 - 196,515 = 3,485). So 924,912 - 3,485.\n\nCalculating that: 924,912 minus 3,000 is 921,912. Then subtract 485 more: 921,912 - 485 = 921,427. Okay, same result. So that confirms it.\n\nTherefore, the sum is indeed 921,427.\n</think>\n\n",
