=11 \u2192 write 1, carryover 1\n\nTen thousands:0+4 +1 (carryover) =5\n\nHundred thousands:4+3=7\n\nSo the total is 751,975. \n\nWait, but let me add them numerically to confirm:\n\n405,361 + 346,614. Let's compute:\n\n400,000 + 300,000 = 700,000\n\n5,000 + 40,000 = 45,000 \u2192 total so far 745,000\n\n300 + 600 = 900 \u2192 745,900\n\n60 + 10 =70 \u2192 745,970\n\n1 +4 =5 \u2192 total 745,975. Wait, that's different again. Wait, this method is conflicting with the previous one. \n\nWait, perhaps I made a mistake in breaking it down. Let me do it step by step properly:\n\n405,361 is 400,000 + 5,000 + 300 + 60 +1\n\n346,614 is 300,000 +40,000 +6,000 +600 +10 +4\n\nAdding each part:\n\n400,000 +300,000 =700,000\n\n5,000 +40,000 =45,000 \u2192 total 745,000\n\n6,000 (from second number) added to the 5,000? Wait no, the first number has 5,000 and the second has 6,000 in thousands place. Wait, let me re-express:\n\nWait, perhaps breaking down each digit:\n\nHundred thousands:\n\n4 (from first) +3 (second) =7 \u2192 700,000\n\nTen thousands:\n\n0 (first) +4 (second) =4 \u2192 40,000\n\nThousands:\n\n5 (first) +6 (second) =11 \u2192 11,000\n\nHundreds:\n\n3 (first) +6 (second) =9 \u2192900\n\nTens:\n\n6 (first) +1 (second) =7 \u219270\n\nOnes:\n\n1 +4 =5 \u21925\n\nNow adding all these components:\n\n700,000 +40,000 =740,000\n\n740,000 +11,000 =751,000\n\n751,000 +900 =751,900\n\n751,900 +70 =751,970\n\n751,970 +5 =751,975. \n\nOkay, so that's consistent with the vertical addition with carryover. So the correct answer is 751,975. \n\nBut in my first calculation, I incorrectly added the thousands place as 5+4 instead of 5+6, leading me to an incorrect 769,975. So I need to correct that. \n\nTherefore, the correct sum is 751,975. Let me confirm once more with another method. \n\nAlternatively, adding the numbers directly:\n\n405,361\n\n+346,614\n\n------------\n\nAdding the numbers step by step:\n\nStart from the right:\n\nOnes:1+4=5\n\nTens:6+1=7\n\nHundreds:3+6=9\n\nThou