ning? Let me check again.\n\nWait in the first time I thought the thousands place was 2+6=8, but the thousands digit in the first number is 2 (from 122,559: the digits are 1 (hundred thousand), 2 (ten thousand), 2 (thousand), 5 (hundred), 5 (ten), 9 (one). The second number's thousands digit is 6 (since it's 766,246: 7 (hundred thousand), 6 (ten thousand), 6 (thousand), 2 (hundred), 4 (ten), 6 (one). So 2 (thousands place from first) +6 (thousands from second) =8. So that's correct. Then the ten thousands place: 2 +6=8. Hundred thousands:1+7=8. So the digits are 8 (hundred thousand), 8 (ten thousand), 8 (thousand), 8 (hundred?), wait no. Wait the hundreds place was 5 (from first) +2 (from second) plus the carryover from tens? Wait the hundreds place: first number's hundreds digit is 5, second's is 2. The carryover from the tens place was 1, so 5+2+1=8. So hundreds digit is 8. Then thousands place: first number's thousands digit is 2, second's is 6, so 2+6=8. So thousands digit is 8. Ten thousands: 2+6=8. Hundred thousands:1+7=8. So the digits from left to right are 8 (hundred thousand), 8 (ten thousand), 8 (thousand), 8 (hundred), 0 (ten), 5 (one). So the number is 888,805. So the correct answer is 888,805. I must have made a typo in my initial thought when I first wrote 888,705. So the final answer should be 888,805. Let me confirm once more with another method. Let's add 122,559 + 766,246.\n\nBreaking into parts:\n\n122,559 + 766,246\n\n= (100,000 + 20,000 + 2,000 + 500 + 50 +9) + (700,000 +60,000 +6,000 +200 +40 +6)\n\nAdding each place:\n\nHundred thousands: 100k +700k =800k\n\nTen thousands:20k +60k=80k\n\nThousands:2k +6k=8k\n\nHundreds:500 +200=700\n\nTens:50 +40=90\n\nOnes:9+6=15\n\nNow add all together:\n\n800,000 +80,000 =880,000\n\n880,000 +8,000=888,000\n\n888,000 +700=888,700\n\n888,700 +90=888,790\n\n888,790 +15=888,805. Yes, that matches. So the correct answer is 888,805. I must have made a mistake in my first calculation when I thought I got 888,705.