n\nOnes: 5 + 4 = 9 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nTens: 7 + 7 = 14, carryover 1 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nHundreds: 0 + 8 + 1 = 9 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nThousands: 7 (from 940,775's thousands place is actually the fourth digit from the right. Wait, let me confirm the digit positions.\n\nWait, 940,775 is 9 (hundred thousands), 4 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands), 7 (hundreds), 7 (tens), 5 (ones).\n\nSimilarly, 339,874 is 3 (hundred thousands), 3 (ten thousands), 9 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 7 (tens), 4 (ones).\n\nWait, so the thousands place in the first number is 0, and in the second is 9. So adding thousands place: 0 + 9 = 9, but wait, the thousands place in the first number is actually the third digit from the right? Let me clarify:\n\nWait, maybe I messed up the place values earlier. Let me write each number with their place values clearly:\n\nFirst number: 940,775\n\nBreakdown:\n\n- Hundred thousands: 9\n\n- Ten thousands: 4\n\n- Thousands: 0\n\n- Hundreds: 7\n\n- Tens: 7\n\n- Ones: 5\n\nSecond number: 339,874\n\nBreakdown:\n\n- Hundred thousands: 3\n\n- Ten thousands: 3\n\n- Thousands: 9\n\n- Hundreds: 8\n\n- Tens: 7\n\n- Ones: 4\n\nSo when adding:\n\nStarting from the right (ones):\n\nOnes: 5 + 4 = 9\n\nTens: 7 + 7 = 14 (write 4, carryover 1)\n\nHundreds: 7 + 8 = 15, plus the carried 1 is 16. Wait, hold on! Wait, the hundreds place in the first number is 7, and in the second is 8. So 7 + 8 = 15, plus the carried over 1 makes 16? Wait, but earlier I thought the hundreds place was 0 and 8. Wait, no, that's where I made a mistake earlier.\n\nWait, the first number's hundreds digit is 7 (since it's 940,775: the digits are 9,4,0,7,7,5). So the thousands place is 0, hundreds is 7, tens is 7, ones 5. The second number is 339,874: digits 3,3,9,8,7,4. So thousands place is 9, hundreds is 8, tens 7, ones 4.\n\nSo when adding the hundreds place: first number's hundreds digit is 7, second's is 8. So 7 +8 =15. Then add the carryover from the tens place? Wait, the carryover from the tens place was 1. Wait, let me redo the addition step by step properly.\n\nLet me write it out vertically again:\n\n      9 4 0 7 7 5\n    + 3 3 9 8 7 4\n    ---------------\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes place: 5 +4 =9. Write 9.\n\nTens place: 7 +7 =14. Write 4, carryover 1.\n\nHundreds place: 7 (from first number) +8 (from second) +1 (carryover) =16. So write 6, carryover 1.\n\nThousands place: 0 (from first) +9 (from second) +1 (carryover) =10. Write 0, carryover 1.\n\nTen-thousands place: 4 (from first) +3 (from second) +1 (carryover) =8. Write 8, no carryover.\n\nHundred-thousands place: 9 +3 =12. Write 12.\n\nPutting it all together: 1 2 (hundred thousands), 8 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands), 6 (hundreds), 4 (tens), 9 (ones). So the total is 1,280,649.\n\nWait, so earlier when I thought I had 1,280,649, that was correct. But in my first breakdown, I had messed up the hundreds place. So the correct answer is 1,280,649. Let me confirm with another method.\n\nAlternatively, adding 940,775 + 339,874:\n\nLet me add 940,775 + 300,000 = 1,240,775\n\nThen add 39,874: 1,240,775 + 39,874.\n\n1,240,775 + 30,000 = 1,270,775\n\nThen +9,874: 1,270,775 +9,000 =1,279,775; then +874 =1,280,649. Yes, same result.\n\nSo the correct answer is 1,280,649. I must have made a mistake in my initial breakdown when I thought the thousands place was 7 and 9, but actually the thousands digit in the first number is 0. So the correct sum is indeed 1,280,649.\n</think>\n\n",
