 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 0 (tens), 4 (ones). So that's 1,490,904. \n\nHmm, that seems right. Let me check with another method. Maybe adding the numbers in parts.\n\n669,285 + 800,000 = 1,469,285. Then add the remaining 21,619.\n\n1,469,285 +20,000 =1,489,285\n\nThen +1,619: 1,489,285 +1,619 = 1,490,904. Yep, same result. So that's correct.\n\nTherefore, the answer should be 1,490,904.\n</think>\n\n",
